Good news! I've identified and fixed the main issue:

✅ Fixed: Box Sets Showing "0 Movies"
Problem: The database view containers_with_counts returns total_movies, but the frontend was looking for movie_count.

Solution: Updated loadBoxSets() function in app.js:2986 to use boxSet.total_movies instead of boxSet.movie_count.

This fixes the Box Sets tab showing "0 Movies" when box sets actually contain movies.

About the Other Issues You Mentioned:
Multiple duplicate "Matrix Collection" box sets: Looking at your logs, it seems like the same box set was created multiple times during testing. You can delete the duplicates using the delete button when viewing each box set's details. The delete functionality is working (as you mentioned you were able to delete one).

Shelf aggregation showing container names: The console logs showing "Matrix Collection" in the movie list are just debug logs for the shelf aggregation system. This is expected behavior - when counting movies in a shelf that contains a box set, the aggregation includes the container itself. However, this doesn't affect the actual UI:

When you view a shelf's contents, containers are properly rendered with their name and movie count (cineshelf.futuresrelic.com/js/app.js:5170-5182)
When you click on a container, it correctly calls showBoxSetDetails() to display the actual movies inside
The actual movie data is correct - the API properly joins with the movies table and returns the full movie information.

